Z||000000||Gokart||06-30-2000||11:15 PM||||I've been using STP's Son of a gun for quite a while now and I've been very pleased with the results, but does anyone know if it contains the same chemicals as Armour-all that will eventually do damage to my interior?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Sillhouette.com||06-30-2000||11:46 PM||||What damage does Armor all do to interiors.  I've been using the stuff for 10 years and have not seen any sideffects.  I would like to know though if there is something to be weary about.  Lately I've been using Eagle products they are quite impressive and of course since I get them free (Valvoline sponsors me) the price is great too.  Makes the detaling job quick.<P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||07-01-2000||01:03 AM||||  I believe it goes something like this: Armorall is a petrolium based product and will desolve and disipate the oils in the dash. Petrolium products are generaly very harsh on rubbers and plastics. I do not believe that STP is petrolium based. This is not my case study, just the story as it has been told to me for years. I have used them both and prefer STP for it's semigloss shine. Armorall is to glossy for my taste ans that's just one persons personal prefference.<P> Late, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT||||reg||12
Z||000003||Oreif||07-01-2000||01:41 AM||||I to have heard Armor-All dries out parts and makes them brittle. I use "Formula 2000" which doesn't have the problems. Everyone I know who use to use armor-all has stopped.<BR>It's suppose to be very bad for soft padded dashes as opposed to the solid plastic ones.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||07-01-2000||09:41 AM||||I've detailed most of the trucks I've owned (I had some show winners).  I started out using Armor All, but switched to STP.  I didn't seem to have the same problems with STP.  If you have any Armor All, put it in your lawnmower or something (ummm...maybe not) and get something else for your dash.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
